Hi Jacob --

It looks like you're using a non-Windows R. You probably need to
re-configure R to build a shared library, and then to re-make R. Do
this with something like

./configure --enable-R-shlib
make

to build R in the source tree (better to build R 'out-of-tree', though
by first making a directory in some convenient location, cd to the
directory, then path/to/R source/configure --enable-R-shlib and make).

See configure --help for more options, and the R installation and
administration manual, section 2, e.g., at

http://cran.fhcrc.org/doc/manuals/R-admin.html

for more information.

Hope that helps,

Martin

